From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:24:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] t31: read a whole frame per T31_AI_GET_STREAM call

dsp_ioctl_ai_stream() only completes when a whole DMA period is ready
and the read is a multiple of the fragment size. Issuing one ioctl per
960-byte fragment means the second fragment of each 20 ms frame waits
for the next period, so a frame takes ~40 ms instead of ~20 ms and the
capture runs at half rate: prudynt then feeds the AAC encoder 24 kHz
of samples while the client expects 48 kHz, giving the audio underruns,
PTS gaps and A-V desync.

Request the whole frame (a multiple of the fragment size) in a single
ioctl, and fall back to one fragment per call only when the remaining
size is not fragment-aligned.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>

---
--- a/src/t31/openimp_t31_audio.c
+++ b/src/t31/openimp_t31_audio.c
@@ -400,12 +400,20 @@
         t31_audio.capture_capacity = capacity;
     }
     while (t31_audio.capture_valid < required) {
+        size_t want = required - t31_audio.capture_valid;
+        if (want > chunk && (want % chunk) == 0) {
+            /* Read the whole frame in one request: the driver only signals a
+             * completed period every fragment_size, so issuing one ioctl per
+             * fragment halves the delivered rate. */
+        } else {
+            want = chunk;
+        }
         memset(&stream, 0, sizeof(stream));
         stream.data = t31_audio.capture_buffer + t31_audio.capture_valid;
-        stream.size = chunk;
+        stream.size = (uint32_t)want;
         if (ioctl(t31_audio.ai_fd, T31_AI_GET_STREAM, &stream) != 0)
             return -1;
-        t31_audio.capture_valid += chunk;
+        t31_audio.capture_valid += want;
     }
     return 0;
 }
